# Copy to `.env` for local overrides. Never commit a real token.
# All of these are optional; sane defaults are used when unset.

# Bind address / port for the embedded server.
MOTHER_CLAUDE_HOST=0.0.0.0
MOTHER_CLAUDE_PORT=6725

# Override the Claude config dir of the Default account (defaults to
# ~/.claude). More accounts — a token used with this directory, or a directory
# of their own like ~/.claude-work — are added in the app under Settings →
# Accounts (docs/ACCOUNTS.md), never here.
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/you/.claude

# Token accounts' tokens and the backup passphrase live in the macOS Keychain
# (service dev.motherclaude.desktop). `file` keeps them in 0600 files in the
# app data dir instead (elsewhere than macOS that is always the case).
# MOTHER_CLAUDE_SECRET_STORE=file

# Credentials are generated at runtime in the app data dir and are never passed
# to claude child processes. Phones pair with one-time codes and get their own
# revocable device tokens (docs/REMOTE.md); hooks use a separate, per-launch
# hook token. Nothing here needs a token value.

# --- Claude HTTP bridge (docs/BRIDGE.md) -----------------------------------
# Programmatic HTTP access to Claude on this machine. Always mounted at /v1 on
# the main server; these control the dedicated loopback listener.

# The API does not start with the app — open the API screen, choose defaults and
# press Start. Set AUTOSTART=1 for headless or CI runs where nobody can.
# MOTHER_CLAUDE_BRIDGE=1                # 0 disables the bridge entirely
# MOTHER_CLAUDE_BRIDGE_AUTOSTART=0      # 1 = start it at launch with plain defaults;
#                                       # all = every API server saved on the API screen
#                                       #       too, each closed to tunnels
# MOTHER_CLAUDE_BRIDGE_ACCOUNT=         # the autostarted API's account: an id or a name
#                                       # (one that does not exist starts nothing)
# MOTHER_CLAUDE_BRIDGE_ACCOUNT_ONLY=0   # 1 = it runs as that account only
# MOTHER_CLAUDE_BRIDGE_PORT=5612        # 0 = no dedicated port, /v1 only
# MOTHER_CLAUDE_BRIDGE_CWD=             # default working directory for new conversations
#
# More API servers — one per account, if you like — are added on the API screen,
# each on a loopback port of its own (5613, 5614, …) and also reachable at
# /servers/<id>/ on 5612 (docs/BRIDGE.md, "Several API servers"). The token
# rules below hold for each of them, port by port — except that `never` is the
# main server's starting position only: an added server starts closed to tunnels.

# The loopback API port is OPEN by default: no bearer token, any browser origin,
# so local tools just work. It never binds an external interface, and the LAN
# mount (/v1 on 6725) always requires the token. To close it down:
# MOTHER_CLAUDE_BRIDGE_REQUIRE_TOKEN=1                        # require the token here too
#
# Or open it the other way: the API screen's "Open to tunnels" switch (under
# Access) drops the token for EVERYONE who can reach 5612 — through a tunnel too
# (ngrok http 5612, cloudflared, …), where the default switches tokenless access
# off. Anyone with the tunnel's URL can then start conversations and approve
# Claude's ordinary tool calls on this Mac. Dangerous actions (bypassPermissions,
# deleting transcripts, dangerous tool approvals) still need a caller on this
# Mac — and none counts as one while a tunnel points at the port. The LAN mount
# (/v1 on 6725) keeps its token. `never` starts every launch with the switch on;
# 0 / off / unset is the default described above.
# MOTHER_CLAUDE_BRIDGE_REQUIRE_TOKEN=never
# MOTHER_CLAUDE_BRIDGE_ORIGINS=http://localhost:4200          # strict browser allowlist

# Enables the direct Messages API routes (/messages, /files): vision,
# vision-coordinates, the Files API and programmatic tool calling. Conversation
# endpoints do NOT need this — they use your Claude Code sign-in.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
